                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "234994100",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198324952178",
                            "num_reviews": 5,
                            "playtime_forever": 1219,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 1219,
                            "last_played": 1789114666
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The gameplay is clunky and clearly lacking in some areas but I actually enjoyed this one. My main complaint would be that the game doesn't control very well. It's forgivable being a smaller indie title but it did take a bit of getting used to. I also experienced a bug where I got stuck out of bounds on the beginning of a chapter but luckily you can skip to any chapter. Story wise, the game is what you'd expect from a Silent Hill inspired game. I found it compelling even though it isn't wholly original. I would recommend so long as you have reasonable expectations. I don't think 6 hours with this game will make you regret being born. The game is better than I'm making it sound. Give it a try. Make a YouTube video about it or something. I wish there was more discussion regarding this game. It deserves that much. Go play it!",
